bin/
obj/
.vs/
.idea/
*.user

# Zips built for upload or hand-off. Windows names a "Send to > Compressed folder"
# zip after the last-selected item, so these turn up under surprising names.
*.zip

# Symbols are never worth carrying. This also covers refs/*.pdb — the framework
# reference assemblies ship without symbols, and there would be nothing to step
# into if they had them.
*.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# refs/ IS COMMITTED, deliberately — the .dll and .xml files both.
#
# They are .NET REFERENCE assemblies: the framework's public API with no method
# bodies. They compile and they give full IntelliSense, and the runtime refuses
# to load them, so publishing them in this public repository does not publish the
# implementation. A kit that opens to a screen of red squiggles has failed before
# anyone has read a line of it, which is why they are here rather than fetched.
#
# The .xml documentation files matter most of all: they are how an AI coding
# assistant learns the framework API. Never ignore them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
